      ],
      "correctAnswer": 1,
      "explanation": "To find the y-intercept, we set x = 0.<br>y = a<span style='vertical-align: super; font-size: 0.75em;'>0</span><br>Any non-zero number raised to the power of 0 is 1. Therefore, y = 1. The y-intercept is the point (0, 1), so the value is <b>1</b>.",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "points": 1
    },
    {
      "id": 1795857681208.4158,
      "question": "<div style='font-size: 1.2em; font-weight: 600;'>If <b>0 < a < 1</b>, the graph of <b>y = a<span style='vertical-align: super; font-size: 0.75em;'>x</span></b> is:</div>",
      "options": [
