      "correctAnswer": 1,
      "explanation": "When the base 'a' is a fraction between 0 and 1 (e.g., y = (1/2)<span style='vertical-align: super; font-size: 0.75em;'>x</span>), the function represents exponential decay. As x increases, the value of y gets smaller. Therefore, the graph is strictly <b>decreasing</b>.",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "points": 1
    },
    {
      "id": 1795857681208.7969,
      "question": "<div style='font-size: 1.2em; font-weight: 600;'>The number <b>e</b> is defined as the limit of:</div>",
