      ],
      "correctAnswer": 0,
      "explanation": "The mathematical constant e (Euler's number) is fundamentally defined as the limit of <b>(1 + 1/n)<span style='vertical-align: super; font-size: 0.75em;'>n</span></b> as n approaches infinity. It is approximately equal to 2.71828.",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "points": 1
    },
    {
      "id": 1795857681208.3906,
      "question": "<div style='font-size: 1.2em; font-weight: 600;'>For <b>y = a<span style='vertical-align: super; font-size: 0.75em;'>x</span></b>, a > 1, as x decreases through negative values, the graph:</div>",
