        "rises rapidly",
        "becomes vertical"
      ],
      "correctAnswer": 1,
      "explanation": "As x takes on larger and larger negative values (e.g., x = &minus;10, &minus;100), a<span style='vertical-align: super; font-size: 0.75em;'>x</span> becomes a very small positive fraction (e.g., a<span style='vertical-align: super; font-size: 0.75em;'>&minus;10</span> = 1 / a<span style='vertical-align: super; font-size: 0.75em;'>10</span>). The graph gets infinitely close to the x-axis (y=0) but <b>never actually intersects it</b>, creating a horizontal asymptote.",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "points": 1
    },
    {
      "id": 1795857681208.656,
      "question": "<div style='font-size: 1.2em; font-weight: 600;'>The domain of <b>y = a<span style='vertical-align: super; font-size: 0.75em;'>x</span></b>, a > 0, a &ne; 1, is:</div>",
      "options": [
