      "correctAnswer": 0,
      "explanation": "Rewrite 1 as log<span style='vertical-align: sub; font-size: 0.75em;'>6</span> 6 and combine the right side using log laws:<br>log<span style='vertical-align: sub; font-size: 0.75em;'>6</span>(x+9) = log<span style='vertical-align: sub; font-size: 0.75em;'>6</span> 6 + log<span style='vertical-align: sub; font-size: 0.75em;'>6</span>(x+3) &minus; log<span style='vertical-align: sub; font-size: 0.75em;'>6</span>(x+2)<br>log<span style='vertical-align: sub; font-size: 0.75em;'>6</span>(x+9) = log<span style='vertical-align: sub; font-size: 0.75em;'>6</span>( 6(x+3) / (x+2) )<br>Equate the arguments:<br>x + 9 = (6x + 18) / (x + 2)<br>Cross-multiply:<br>(x + 9)(x + 2) = 6x + 18<br>x<span style='vertical-align: super; font-size: 0.75em;'>2</span> + 11x + 18 = 6x + 18<br>x<span style='vertical-align: super; font-size: 0.75em;'>2</span> + 5x = 0<br>x(x + 5) = 0<br>x = 0 or x = &minus;5.<br>Check the domain: x+9 > 0, x+3 > 0, x+2 > 0, so x > &minus;2.<br>Therefore, x = &minus;5 is rejected. The solution is <b>x = 0</b>.",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "points": 1
